cat > "$CLAUDE_JOB_DIR/tmp/body.txt" <<'EOF'
Hi all,

I don't think we should close this out. I think that would be the wrong call for the building.

I'd put this to us as a "when," not an "if." EV-ready infrastructure is already standard in new Victorian builds, adoption keeps climbing, and the cost of fitting a building like ours won't fall over time.

The contribution to the backbone is modest. By liability it works out to about $22 per entitlement unit, so roughly $1,060 for the smallest lot up to around $2,730 for the largest, as a one-off. Weigh that against what it protects. EV-readiness is fast becoming something buyers and renters look for, and a building that has it will show better than comparable stock that doesn't. If we decline, the real cost turns up later in weaker sale prices and softer rental demand across every lot. That hits all of us, EV owner or not, and it dwarfs the one-off contribution.

The $125k is also only indicative. We haven't asked Origin for the firm quote they offered, and Kimmi's right that we should see what other providers come back with.

Rather than walk away, I'd like us to put a few questions to Origin and to ourselves first:

- Is there a cheaper alternative, from Origin or a competitor?
- Could the resident cost be staged over a few years instead of paid up front?
- Can the OC absorb the backbone over time, or could Origin offer an instalment plan?
- Is a staged rollout viable, part of the capacity now and the rest as we approach it, to spread the cost further?

Closing this out without even asking those questions does every owner a disservice, and I think it leaves money on the table for all of us in the long run.

I'll do the legwork on the quotes and these questions if there's appetite for it.

Thanks,
Nick
EOF
bun -e '
const fs=require("fs");
const body=fs.readFileSync(process.env.CLAUDE_JOB_DIR+"/tmp/body.txt","utf8");
const to="james.ma@amity.com.au";
const cc="scottywalkz@hotmail.com,tssmark@yahoo.com,kimmi19804@hotmail.com";
const subject="Re: 728653T - 40-44 Pakington Street St Kilda - Feasibility study on the installation of EV Chargers";
const q=(s)=>encodeURIComponent(s);
const url=`https://outlook.live.com/mail/0/deeplink/compose?to=${q(to)}&cc=${q(cc)}&subject=${q(subject)}&body=${q(body)}`;
fs.writeFileSync(process.env.CLAUDE_JOB_DIR+"/tmp/link.txt",url);
console.log("LINK_LENGTH:",url.length);
'
echo "---LINK---"
cat "$CLAUDE_JOB_DIR/tmp/link.txt"

cat > "$CLAUDE_JOB_DIR/tmp/ev_draft.applescript" <<'APPLESCRIPT'
set theBody to (read POSIX file "/tmp/ev_body.txt")
tell application "Microsoft Outlook"
	set newMsg to make new outgoing message with properties {subject:"Re: 728653T - 40-44 Pakington Street St Kilda - Feasibility study on the installation of EV Chargers", content:theBody}
	make new recipient at newMsg with properties {email address:{address:"james.ma@amity.com.au"}}
	make new cc recipient at newMsg with properties {email address:{address:"scottywalkz@hotmail.com"}}
	make new cc recipient at newMsg with properties {email address:{address:"tssmark@yahoo.com"}}
	make new cc recipient at newMsg with properties {email address:{address:"kimmi19804@hotmail.com"}}
	open newMsg
	activate
end tell
return "DRAFT_CREATED"
APPLESCRIPT
ssh mac 'cat > /tmp/ev_draft.applescript' < "$CLAUDE_JOB_DIR/tmp/ev_draft.applescript"
ssh mac 'osascript /tmp/ev_draft.applescript' 2>&1
